(Bug #110, boolean. The slot must resolve `'flagged'` and render it exactly
 as the bare `{flagged}` form does - whatever that rendering is - since a
 single-word quoted identifier is the same token as its bare form
 (LANGUAGE.md:711 rule 4), not a different one that happens to print
 differently.)

a boolean called 'flagged' is yes.
Print "{flagged}".
Print "{'flagged'}".
